## 2. Annual Objectives and Key Results (FY 2024)

The following OKRs define the Engineering Department's priorities for the year.

### Objective 1: Drive Product Excellence and Customer Satisfaction

**Goal:** Significantly enhance the quality, reliability, and user experience across all four MedSync product lines to solidify market leadership and customer loyalty.

| Key Result (KR) | Target | Stretch | Alignment |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| KR 1.1: Increase the overall Company Net Promoter Score (NPS) from 71 to **75** by Q4 2024. | 75 | 77 | Customer Success, Product |
| KR 1.2: Reduce critical production incidents (P1/P2) by **40%** compared to Q4 2023. | 40% | 50% | Operational Stability |
| KR 1.3: Achieve a Net Revenue Retention (NRR) of **120%** for all product lines. | 120% | 125% | Financial Growth (Current NRR is 118% [1]) |
| KR 1.4: Improve the average product NPS for MedSync Analytics from 68 to **72**. | 72 | 74 | Product Quality (Analytics is the lowest-scoring product [1]) |

### Objective 2: Scale Platform Infrastructure for Growth and Efficiency

**Goal:** Prepare the MedSync platform for massive scale, ensuring cost-efficiency and technical readiness to support the next phase of customer acquisition and product development.

| Key Result (KR) | Target | Stretch | Alignment |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| KR 2.1: Reduce the average cost per transaction (CPT) by **15%** through cloud optimization and re-architecture. | 15% | 20% | Financial Efficiency |
| KR 2.2: Acquire 500 new hospital clients (Target: **450**, Stretch: **600**). | 450 | 600 | Sales & Business Development (Current Hospital Count is 520 [1]) |
| KR 2.3: Complete the migration of the MedSync Patient Portal to the new microservices architecture, achieving **100%** completion. | 100% | 100% | Technical Debt, Product |
| KR 2.4: Increase platform uptime to **99.99%** (no more than 52 minutes of unplanned downtime annually). | 99.99% | 99.999% | Reliability, Compliance |

### Objective 3: Cultivate a High-Performing and Sustainable Engineering Culture

**Goal:** Invest in the team's capabilities and well-being to ensure the Engineering Department remains a top-tier organization capable of executing on ambitious product and platform goals.

| Key Result (KR) | Target | Stretch | Alignment |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| KR 3.1: Reduce the voluntary attrition rate from 12.5% to **8.0%** by Q4 2024. | 8.0% | 7.0% | HR & People (Current Voluntary Attrition is 12.5% [1]) |
| KR 3.2: Achieve an average of **40** hours of professional development/training per engineer. | 40 | 50 | Talent Development |
| KR 3.3: Increase the Engineering team's diversity (gender and underrepresented groups) by **10%** across all levels. | 10% | 15% | HR & People |
| KR 3.4: Fill **95%** of all open Engineering roles within 45 days of posting. | 95% | 100% | Recruitment Efficiency |

